2. Freeciv — GPL-2.0-or-later — https://github.com/freeciv/freeciv
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
(This section covers the first of the two checked-in third-party data items;
the second, an eight-entry direction table from CivRealm, is §4.)

Freeciv is the game underneath CivRealm. Its rulesets ship human-readable
helptext for technologies, units, and improvements.

Verbatim Freeciv ruleset helptext is **checked into this repository**, inside
the first-turn `raw_snapshot` field of six play-loop transcripts:

    playloop/runs/constrained-smoke2/transcript.json
    playloop/runs/local-llama1b-50turn/transcript.json
    playloop/runs/local-llama1b-schema/transcript.json
    playloop/runs/main/transcript.json
    playloop/runs/sonnet-baseline/transcript.json
    playloop/runs/sonnet-fixed/transcript.json

Each of those files carries roughly 0.22 MB of raw snapshot, of which about
27 KB across ~115 `helptext` fields is verbatim Freeciv prose (e.g. "The
Carrier is a mobile airport."). That text is Freeciv's, licensed
GPL-2.0-or-later, and redistributing these files redistributes it. It is
captured observation data, not code, and it is not used by anything at
runtime — see the "Transcript raw_snapshot" note in README.md.


3. freeciv-web — AGPL-3.0 — https://github.com/freeciv/freeciv-web
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
freeciv-web is the game server CivRealm talks to. This project neither
contains nor modifies any part of it; SETUP.md instructs the user to run the
stock upstream image as a **separate process**, reached over the network:

    docker run -d --name freeciv-web --rm -p 8080:80 freeciv/freeciv-web:latest

Because it is a separate program communicating at arm's length over a
network protocol, it is not combined with this code, and the AGPL does not
reach this repository. AGPL-3.0 §13's obligation — to offer users interacting
with the server over a network the corresponding source of the version they
are running — falls on whoever operates a **modified** freeciv-web. Running
the unmodified upstream image locally adds no obligation beyond what upstream
already satisfies.


4. One transcribed fact table from CivRealm
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
`GOTO_TO_COMPASS` in `src/civrealm_mcp/core.py` maps CivRealm's eight
`goto_<n>` action keys to compass directions:

    goto_0 -> move_NorthWest, goto_1 -> move_North, ... goto_7 -> move_SouthEast

Those eight pairings were read off CivRealm's own
`configs/llm_wrapper_settings.yaml` — they have to match it exactly or the
compass annotations this repo shows a model would be wrong — and the source is
named in a comment at the definition. It is a bare correspondence table, not
code: no CivRealm source is copied, and nothing about how CivRealm computes or
executes a move is reproduced. It is called out here only so that "no
third-party source code is vendored" is not read as "nothing at all was taken
from upstream".


